{"story_id": "conf_s001", "qid": "conf_s001_q3", "qtype": "Q3", "arm": "C", "level": 0.3, "pass1_raw": null, "raw": "<|channel>thought\nthought\n<channel|>To determine which events would no longer occur if E2 did not happen, we evaluate the dependencies for each event (excluding E2):\n\n1.  **E1**: Root event; occurs regardless of E2.\n2.  **E3**: Requires E1 (AND). Since E1 still occurs, E3 occurs.\n3.  **E4**: Requires E1 OR E2. Since E1 occurs, E4 still occurs.\n4.  **E5**: Requires E1 (AND). Since E1 still occurs, E5 still occurs.\n5.  **E6**: Requires E1 AND E3 (AND). Since E1 and E3 occur, E6 still occurs.\n6.  **E7**: Requires E5 OR E6 (OR). Since both E5 and E6 occur, E7 still occurs.\n7.  **E8**: Requires E2 AND E5 (Note: The text says E8 requires E2, E5 under rule AND; the structured facts say E8 requires E7 under rule AND. Following the text's logic for E8: \"Event E8 requires parent events (E2, E5) under rule AND\"). If E2 does not occur, E8 (requiring E2 AND E5) will not occur.\n\nWait, let's re-check the dependency rules provided in the text for all events:\n- E1: Root (Occurs)\n- E2: Root (Given as not happening)\n- E3: Needs E1 (E1 occurs $\\rightarrow$ E3 occurs)\n- E4: Needs E1 OR E2 (E1 occurs $\\rightarrow$ E4 occurs)\n- E5: Needs E1 (E1 occurs $\\rightarrow$ E5 occurs)\n- E6: Needs E1 AND E3 (E1 and E3 occur $\\rightarrow$ E6 occurs)\n- E7: Needs E5 OR E6 (E5/E6 occur $\\sout{\\rightarrow}$ E7 occurs)\n- E8: Needs E2 AND E5 (E2 does not occur $\\rightarrow$ E8 does **not** occur)\n\nChecking the text vs structured facts for E8:\nText: \"Event E8 requires parent events (E2, E5) under rule AND\"\nStructured Facts: \"DEPENDENCY: E8 requires (E7) with rule", "parsed": null, "gold": ["E8"], "correct": false, "parse_ok": false, "tokens_in": 1393, "tokens_out": 512, "seconds": 5.3767, "seed": 4001, "exposed": true}
