{"story_id": "conf_s023", "qid": "conf_s023_q3", "qtype": "Q3", "arm": "B", "level": 0.3, "pass1_raw": null, "raw": "thought\n<channel|>To determine which events would no longer occur if E2 (anomalous sequence 2) had not happened, we first examine the dependency rules for all listed events:\n\n1.  **E1**: Root event (always occurs).\n2.  **E3**: Root event (always occurs).\n3.  **E4**: Requires E1 (AND rule). Since E1 is a root, E4 occurs.\n4.  **E6**: Requires E1 AND E4. Since E1 and E4 occur, E6 occurs.\n5.  **E7**: Requires E3 OR E4. Since both occur, E7 occurs.\n6.  **E8**: Requires E1 OR E4. Since both occur, E8 occurs.\n7.  **FAKE_E1, FAKE_E2, FAKE_E3**: These are listed as events but have no parents/dependencies defined in the text (they are treated as root events unless stated otherwise).\n\nThe question asks what would happen if **E2** had not happened. Looking at the dependency list:\n- E1, E3, E4, E6, E7, and E8 do not depend on E2.\n- The \"Fake\" events (E1, E2, E3) are listed in the event section but their dependencies are not linked to any other events in the provided text. \n\nSince no events in the list depend on E2, the removal of E2 does not affect the occurrence of any other event.\n\n{\"answer\": []}", "parsed": [], "gold": ["E3"], "correct": false, "parse_ok": true, "tokens_in": 624, "tokens_out": 334, "seconds": 3.3488, "seed": 4023, "exposed": true}
{"story_id": "conf_s023", "qid": "conf_s023_q3", "qtype": "Q3", "arm": "C", "level": 0.3, "pass1_raw": null, "raw": "<|channel>thought\n<channel|>To determine which events (excluding E2) would no longer occur if E2 did not happen, we evaluate the dependency rules provided in the text:\n\n1.  **E1**: Root event; always occurs.\n2.  **E2**: Given as an autonomous root event that always occurs (though the question asks us to assume it does not).\n3.  **E3**: Requires E2 under rule AND. If E2 does not occur, **E3** will not occur.\n4.  **E_4**: Requires E1 under rule AND. Since E1 is a root event and still occurs, E4 still occurs.\n5.  **E5**: Requires E4 under rule AND. Since E4 occurs, E5 still occurs.\n6.  **E6**: Requires (E1, E4) under rule AND. Since both E1 and E4 occur, E6 still occurs.\n7.  **E7**: Requires (E3, E4) under rule OR. If E2 does not happen, E3 does not happen. However, since E4 is still occurring, the OR condition for E7 is satisfied by E4. Thus, E7 still occurs.\n8.  **E8**: Requires (E1, E4) under rule OR. Since both E1 and E4 occur, E8 still occurs.\n\nThe only event (excluding E2) that fails to occur when E2 is removed is E3.\n\n{\"answer\": [\"E3\"]}", "parsed": ["E3"], "gold": ["E3"], "correct": true, "parse_ok": true, "tokens_in": 1307, "tokens_out": 324, "seconds": 3.3374, "seed": 4023, "exposed": true}
