{"story_id": "conf_s032", "qid": "conf_s032_q3", "qtype": "Q3", "arm": "A", "level": 0.0, "pass1_raw": null, "raw": "<|channel>thoughtthought\n<channel|>To determine which events (excluding E1) would no longer occur if E1 did not happen, we evaluate the dependency rules for each event:\n\n1.  **E2**: Autonomous root event. It occurs regardless of E1.\n2.  **E3**: Requires E1 under rule **AND**. If E1 does not occur, E3 cannot occur.\n3.  **E4**: Requires (E2, E3) under rule **OR**. Since E2 is an autonomous root and still occurs, E4 will still occur even if E3/E1 do not.\n4.  **E5**: Requires E4 under rule **AND**. If E4 occurs, E5 occurs. (Note: E4's occurrence depends on E2 or E3; since E2 occurs, E4 occurs, and thus E5 occurs).\n5.  **E6**: Requires (E_1, E4) under rule **OR**. Since E4 occurs, E6 will still occur.\n6.  **E7**: Requires (E1, E2) under rule **OR**. Since E2 is an autonomous root and still occurs, E7 will still occur.\n7.  **E8**: Requires (E4, E6) under rule **OR**. Since both E4 and E6 occur, E8 will still occur.\n\nThe only event (excluding E1) that fails to occur when E1 is removed is E3.\n\n```json\n{\"answer\": [\"E3\"]}\n```", "parsed": ["E3"], "gold": ["E3"], "correct": true, "parse_ok": true, "tokens_in": 900, "tokens_out": 327, "seconds": 3.3876, "seed": 4032, "exposed": false}
