{"story_id": "conf_s032", "qid": "conf_s032_q3", "qtype": "Q3", "arm": "F", "level": 0.0, "pass1_raw": "<|channel>thought\nRelevant Facts:\n- E1 is an autonomous root event (always occurs).\n- E2 is an autonomous root event (always occurs).\n- E3 requires E1 (Rule AND).\n- E4 requires E2 OR E3 (Rule OR).\n- E5 requires E4 (Rule AND).\n- E6 requires E1 OR E4 (Rule OR).\n- E7 requires E1 OR E2 (Rule OR).\n- E_8 requires E4 OR E6 (Rule OR).\n\nHypothetical Condition: E1 does not occur.\n\nPlan:\n1. Identify the immediate impact of E1's absence on its direct dependents using the AND/OR rules.\n2. Trace the chain reaction through the dependency graph to see which subsequent events are affected.\n3. List all-affected event IDs (excluding E1) in a sorted JSON list.\n\nNote: I must check if E4, E6, E7, or E8 still occur via their OR dependencies even if E1 is missing. \n- E3 depends on E1 (AND). If E1 is gone, E3 is gone.\n- E4 depends on", "raw": "<|channel>thought1. E1 is an autonomous root event (always occurs). If we assume E1 does not occur:\n2. E3 requires E1 (AND rule). Since E1 is missing, E3 will not occur.\n3. E4 requires E2 OR E3 (OR rule). E2 is a root event and still occurs. Therefore, E4 still occurs.\n4. E5 requires E4 (AND rule). Since E4 still occurs, we check if E4's parents are satisfied. E4 depends on E2 or E3. E2 occurs, so E4 occurs. E5 depends on E4. Since E4 occurs, E5 occurs.\n5. E6 requires E1 OR E4 (OR rule). Since E4 occurs, E6 still occurs.\n6. E7 requires E1 OR E2 (OR rule). Since E2 occurs, E7 still occurs.\n7. E8 requires E4 OR E6 (OR rule). Since E4 and E6 occur, E8 still occurs.\n8. E2 is a root event and its occurrence is not dependent on E1.\n\nConclusion: Only E3 is lost because it depends on E1 via an AND rule. All other events are either roots or depend on at least one-other occurring event (E2) through OR rules.\n\nWait, let's re-verify:\n- E1: Not happening (given).\n- E2: Root (always occurs).\n- E3: Needs E1 (AND). E1 is gone -> E3 is gone.\n- E4: Needs E2 OR E3 (OR). E2 exists -> E4 happens.\n- E5: Needs E4 (AND). E4 exists -> E5 happens.\n- E6: Needs E1 OR E4 (OR). E4 exists -> E6 happens.\n- E7: Needs E1 OR E2 (OR). E2 exists -> E7 happens.\n- E8: Needs E4 OR E6 (OR). E_4/E6 exist -> E8 happens.\n\nThe only event that fails is E3.\n\nFinal check of the list: [\"E3\"].\n\nWait, let me re-read \"an event with rule AND occurs only if all its listed parents occur\".\nE3's parent is E1. If E1 doesn't happen, E3 doesn'", "parsed": null, "gold": ["E3"], "correct": false, "parse_ok": false, "tokens_in": 3326, "tokens_out": 762, "seconds": 7.8002, "seed": 4032, "exposed": false}
