{"story_id": "conf_s033", "qid": "conf_s033_q3", "qtype": "Q3", "arm": "B", "level": 0.0, "pass1_raw": null, "raw": "thought\n<channel|>To determine which events would no longer occur if E3 did not happen, we evaluate the dependency rules for all other events:\n\n1.  **E1**: Root event (always occurs).\n2.  **E2**: Root event (always occurs).\n3.  **E4**: Requires (E1 OR E2). Since E1 and E2 are roots, E4 still occurs regardless of E3.\n4.  **E5**: Requires (E1 AND E4). Since E1 and E4 occur, E5 still occurs.\n5.  **E6**: Requires (E3 AND E4). If E3 does not happen, the \"AND\" condition for E6 is not met. Therefore, **E6** will no longer occur.\n6.  **E7**: Requires (E1 AND E4). Since E1 and E4 occur, E7 still occurs.\n7.  **E8**: Requires (E1 AND E2). Since E1 and E2 are roots, E8 still occurs.\n\nThe only event (excluding E3) that depends on E3 via an AND rule is E6.\n\n{\"answer\": [\"E6\"]}", "parsed": ["E6"], "gold": ["E6"], "correct": true, "parse_ok": true, "tokens_in": 884, "tokens_out": 255, "seconds": 2.6622, "seed": 4033, "exposed": false}
{"story_id": "conf_s033", "qid": "conf_s033_q3", "qtype": "Q3", "arm": "C", "level": 0.0, "pass1_raw": null, "raw": "<|channel>thought\n\u0633\u0627\u0632\u06cc-thought\n<channel|>To determine which events would no longer occur if E3 did not happen, we evaluate the dependency rules for all other events:\n\n1.  **E1**: Root event (always occurs).\n2.  **E2**: Root event (always occurs).\n3.  **E4**: Requires (E1, E2) under rule OR. Since E1 and E2 occur, E4 still occurs.\n4.  **E5**: Requires (E1, E4) under rule AND. Since E1 and E4 occur, E5 still occurs.\n5.  **E6**: Requires (E3, E4) under rule AND. Since E3 is now-denied, the AND condition fails. **E6 will not occur**.\n6.  **E7**: Requires (E1, E4) under rule AND. Since E1 and E4 occur, E7 still occurs.\n7.  **E8**: Requires (E1, E2) under rule AND. Since E1 and E2 occur, E8 still contains its parents.\n\nWait, let's re-check if any other events depend on E6 or E7:\n- E6 is a parent for nothing listed in the rules.\n- E7 is a parent for nothing listed in the rules.\n- E3 was a parent for E6. Since E3 did not happen, E6 does not happen.\n\nChecking dependencies again:\n- E1 (Root) -> OK\n- E2 (Root) -> OK\n- E3 (Parent: E1) -> Denied by premise\n- E4 (Parents: E1 OR E2) -> OK\n- E5 (Parents: E1 AND E4) -> OK\n- E6 (Parents: E3 AND E4) -> **E3 is missing, so E6 fails.**\n- E7 (Parents: E1 AND E4) -> OK\n- E8 (Parents: E1 AND E2) -> OK\n\nOnly E6 is affected by the non-occurrence of E3.\n\n{\"answer\": [\"E6\"]}", "parsed": ["E6"], "gold": ["E6"], "correct": true, "parse_ok": true, "tokens_in": 1577, "tokens_out": 456, "seconds": 4.6498, "seed": 4033, "exposed": false}
