{"story_id": "conf_s033", "qid": "conf_s033_q4", "qtype": "Q4", "arm": "F", "level": 0.3, "pass1_raw": "---\n### Relevant Facts\n**Events & Timelines:**\n*   E1 (Thermal Radiator Deployment): Start 5, Duration 3.\n*   E2 (Cryogenic Manifold Flush): Start 10, Duration 3.\n*   E4 (Subspace Beacon Ping): Start 21, Duration 2.\n\n**Rules & Dependencies:**\n*   Rule [RULE_CR1]: IF Event E1 occurs $\\rightarrow$ telemetry_downlink = high_gain_active.\n\n**Metadata/Telemetry:**\n*   D1: Sub-deck Maintenance Log status is certified normal.\n*   D2: Sector 7 Habitation Ring pressure is 101.3 kPa.\n\n**Question Goal:**\nDetermine the value of `telemetry_downlink` if E1 occurs.\n\n### Plan\n1.  _Identify the specific rule-based condition:_ Locate the conditional rule governing `telemetry_downlink`.\n2.  _Verify Event E1 status:_ Confirm that E1 is an autonomous root event (per [DEP_E1]) and its occurrence triggers the rule.\n3.  _Apply Rule:_ If E1 occurs, set", "raw": "<|channel>thought\n<channel|>To determine the value of `telemetry_downlink`, we look at the rule [RULE_CR1] provided in the text: \"Safety protocol dictates: IF Event E1 occurs, THEN telemetry_downlink is set to high_gain_active\". \n\nAccording to the text, Event E1 (Thermal Radiator Deployment) is an autonomous root event and always occurs ([DEP_E1]). Therefore, the condition for the rule is met.\n\nThe value assigned is \"high_gain_active\".\n\n{\"answer\": \"high_gain_active\"}", "parsed": "high_gain_active", "gold": "high_gain_active", "correct": true, "parse_ok": true, "tokens_in": 2730, "tokens_out": 371, "seconds": 4.0365, "seed": 4033, "exposed": true}
