{"story_id": "conf_s062", "qid": "conf_s062_q3", "qtype": "Q3", "arm": "B", "level": 0.3, "pass1_raw": null, "raw": "<|channel>thoughtthought\nE1 is an event that occurs (it's a ROOT event). If E1 had not happened, we need to check which other events would fail their dependency rules.\n\n- E2: Root event. It does not depend on E1. So E2 still occurs.\n- E3: Requires E1 (AND rule). If E1 doesn't happen, E3 won't happen.\n- E4: Requires E1 (AND rule). If E1 doesn't happen, E4 won't happen.\n- E5: Requires E1 (OR rule). If E1 doesn't happen, we check if other parents exist. E5 has only one parent (E1) in the list. Since it's an OR rule, if E1 is gone, E5 would not occur *unless* there were other parents listed for E5. Looking at the dependencies:\n    - E3 depends on E1.\n    - E\ub85c4 depends on E1.\n    - E5 depends on E1.\n    - E6 depends on (E2, E3) with rule OR. If E1 doesn't happen, E3 won't happen. However, E6 is an OR rule for E2 and E3. Since E2 is a root event and still occurs, E6 will still occur via E2.\n    - E7 depends on (E1, E5) with rule OR. If E1 doesn't happen, we check if E5 happens. But E5 also depends on E1. If E1 doesn't happen, E5 doesn' way happen. If E5 doesn't happen and E1 doesn't happen, E7 (which is an OR rule for E1 and E5) would not occur.\n    - E8 depends on (E1, E4) with rule OR. If E1 doesn't happen, E4 won't happen. Since both parents (E1 and E4) are gone, E8 will not occur.\n\nWait, let me re-evaluate carefully:\nIf E1 is NOT happening:\n1. E3 depends on E1 (AND). E1 is gone -> E3 is gone.\n2. E4 depends on E1 (AND). E1 is gone -> E4 is gone.\n3. E5 depends on E1 (OR). E1 is gone", "parsed": null, "gold": ["E3", "E4", "E5", "E7", "E8"], "correct": false, "parse_ok": false, "tokens_in": 702, "tokens_out": 512, "seconds": 4.9985, "seed": 4062, "exposed": true}
