{"story_id": "conf_s085", "qid": "conf_s085_q2", "qtype": "Q2", "arm": "D", "level": 0.3, "pass1_raw": "<|channel>thought\n<channel|>```json\n[\n  {\n    \"id\": \"EVENT E2\",\n    \"reason\": \"The text defines E2 (Coolant Valve Depressurization) starting at hour 12 with duration 6, but the structured facts omit it entirely.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\":_E3_dependency_logic\",\n    \"reason\": \"Text states E3 requires (E1, E2) under rule AND; Structured Facts state E3 requires only (E1).\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"EVENT E4_dependency_logic\",\n    \"reason\": \"Text states E4 requires (E2, E3) under rule OR; Structured Facts state E4 requires only (E3).\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"EVENT E5_dependency_logic\",\n    \"reason\": \"Text states E5 requires (E2) under rule AND; Structured Facts label E5 as a ROOT event.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"EVENT E6_dependency_logic\",\n    \"reason\": \"Text states E6 requires (E4, E5", "raw": "<|channel>thought\n<channel|>To calculate the total combined duration of E4 and E8, we use the durations provided in the text:\n- Event E4 (Thermal Radiator Deployment) has a duration of 3 hours.\n- Event E8 (Plasma Exhaust Venting) has a duration of 4 hours.\n\nTotal duration = 3 + 4 = 7.\n\n{\"answer\": 7}", "parsed": 7, "gold": 7, "correct": true, "parse_ok": true, "tokens_in": 2763, "tokens_out": 335, "seconds": 3.892, "seed": 4085, "exposed": true}
{"story_id": "conf_s085", "qid": "conf_s085_q2", "qtype": "Q2", "arm": "F", "level": 0.3, "pass1_raw": "<|channel>thought\n<channel|>To answer the question regarding the total combined duration of Event E4 and Event E8, I will use the following extracted facts:\n\n**Relevant Facts:**\n*   **Event E4 (Thermal Radiator Deployment):** Duration = 3 hours (from `[EV_E4]`).\n*   **Event E8 (Plasma Exhaust Venting):** Duration = 4 hours (from `[EV_E8]`).\n*   *Note: The structured facts section contains errors/discrepancies regarding durations and dependencies for these specific events; I will rely on the primary \"MISSION TIMELINE AND LOG\" text which explicitly defines E4 and E8's durations.*\n\n**Plan:**\n1.  Identify the duration of Event E4 from the text.\n2.  Identify the duration of Event E8 from the text.\n3.  Sum the two durations (E4 + E8).\n4.  Provide the result as a single integer.", "raw": "<|channel>thought\n<channel|>{\"answer\": 7}", "parsed": 7, "gold": 7, "correct": true, "parse_ok": true, "tokens_in": 2704, "tokens_out": 218, "seconds": 2.6472, "seed": 4085, "exposed": true}
{"story_id": "conf_s085", "qid": "conf_s085_q3", "qtype": "Q3", "arm": "A", "level": 0.0, "pass1_raw": null, "raw": "thought\n<channel|>To determine which events (excluding E2) would no longer occur if E2 did not happen, we evaluate the dependency rules for each event:\n\n1.  **E1**: Root event; occurs regardless of E2.\n2.  **E3**: Requires (E1 AND E2). If E2 does not occur, E3 does not occur.\n3.  **E4**: Requires (E2 OR E3). Since E3 is now also not occurring (due to the failure of E3's dependency on E2), and E2 is not occurring, E4 will not occur.\n4.  **E5**: Requires (E2) under rule AND. If E2 does not occur, E5 does not occur.\n5.  **E6**: Requires (E4 AND E5). Since E4 and E5 are no longer occurring, E6 will not occur.\n6.  **E7**: Requires (E2 OR E3). Since both E2 and E3 are not occurring, E7 will not occur.\n7.  **E8**: Requires (E1 OR E2). Since E1 is a root event that still occurs, E8 will still occur.\n\nThe events that would no longer occur (excluding E2) are: E3, E4, E5, E6, and E7.\n\nSorting the IDs: [\"E3\", \"E4\", \"E5\", \"E6\", \"E7\"]\n\n{\"answer\": [\"E3\", \"E4\", \"E5\", \"E6\", \"E7\"]}", "parsed": ["E3", "E4", "E5", "E6", "E7"], "gold": ["E3", "E4", "E5", "E6", "E7"], "correct": true, "parse_ok": true, "tokens_in": 901, "tokens_out": 340, "seconds": 3.556, "seed": 4085, "exposed": false}
{"story_id": "conf_s085", "qid": "conf_s085_q3", "qtype": "Q3", "arm": "B", "level": 0.0, "pass1_raw": null, "raw": "thought\n<channel|>To determine which events would no longer occur if E2 did not happen, we evaluate the dependency rules for each event:\n\n1.  **E1**: Root event (always occurs). Status: **Occurs**.\n2.  **E2**: Given as NOT occurring.\n3.  **E3**: Requires (E1 AND E2). Since E2 is not happening, E3 does not occur. Status: **No longer occurs**.\n4.  **E4**: Requires (E2 OR E3). Since E2 is not happening and E3 is not happening, E4 does not occur. Status: **No longer occurs**.\n5.  **E5**: Requires (E2) with rule AND. Since E2 is not happening, E5 does not occur. Status: way **No longer occurs**.\n6.  **E6**: Requires (E4 AND E5). Since both E4 and E5 are no longer occurring, E6 does not occur. Status: **No longer occurs**.\n7.  **E7**: Requires (E2 OR E3). Since E2 is not happening and E3 is not happening, E7 does not occur. Status: **No longer \uc788\uc73c occurs**.\n8.  **E8**: Requires (E1 OR E2). Since E1 still occurs, E8 still occurs. Status: **Occurs**.\n\nThe events that would no longer occur (excluding E2) are E3, E4, E5, E6, and E7. Sorting these IDs: [\"E3\", \"E4\", \"E5\", \"E6\", \"E7\"].\n\n{\"answer\": [\"E3\", \"E4\", \"E5\", \"E6\", \"E7\"]}", "parsed": ["E3", "E4", "E5", "E6", "E7"], "gold": ["E3", "E4", "E5", "E6", "E7"], "correct": true, "parse_ok": true, "tokens_in": 884, "tokens_out": 372, "seconds": 3.8102, "seed": 4085, "exposed": false}
