pends on E3 (which depends on E2). E7 depends on E4 (which depends on E2). \n\nLet's re-evaluate the chain:\n- If E2 is out:\n- E3 (needs E2) -> Out.\n- E4 (needs E1, E2) -> Out.\n- E5 (needs E1, E3) -> Out.\n- E6 (needs E1 OR E5) -> In (because E1 is in).\n- E7 (needs E1 AND E4) -> Out (because E4 is out).\n\nThe list of events that would not occur is: E3, E4, E5, E7. \nWait, let's check the text for E7 again: \"Event E7 requires parent events (E1, E4) under rule AND\". Since E4 is dependent on E2, and E2 is out, E4 is out. Therefore E7 is out", "parsed": null, "gold": ["E3", "E4", "E5", "E7"], "correct": false, "parse_ok": false, "tokens_in": 2943, "tokens_out": 762, "seconds": 7.7634, "seed": 4100, "exposed": true}
